1
00:00:53,900 --> 00:01:10,600
Om. We meditate on the divine Sun's glorious light;
may it awaken our minds.

2
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:54,000
The glory of Mitra, the god who upholds all peoples,
is true, all-winning, and of the brightest renown.

3
00:03:54,100 --> 00:04:05,000
Mitra, knowing all, sets the peoples in order;
Mitra holds up the earth and the sky.

4
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:31,260
I take refuge in the Buddha. I take refuge in the Dharma.
I take refuge in the Sangha.

5
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:44,700
Om. We meditate on the divine Sun's glorious light;
may it awaken our minds.

6
00:05:50,300 --> 00:06:04,900
The winds blow honey-sweet for the righteous,
the rivers run sweet; may the plants be sweet for us.

7
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:19,560
The winds blow honey-sweet for the righteous,
the rivers run sweet; may the plants be sweet for us.

8
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:30,000
Sweet be the night and the dawns, sweet the earth's air;
sweet be Heaven, our father.

9
00:06:30,100 --> 00:06:40,600
Sweet be the trees to us, and sweet the sun;
sweet be the cows to us.

10
00:06:53,800 --> 00:07:01,800
...holding the life-breath at the crown of the head,
steadfast in the discipline of yoga,

11
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:06,300
uttering Om, the one syllable that is Brahman,
and remembering Me,

12
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:10,900
whoever departs, leaving the body,
reaches the highest goal.

13
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:17,500
The supreme Self, the One, the first seed of the world,
free of desire, formless, known through Om.

14
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:15,500
Let my breath return to the deathless wind,
and this body end in ashes.

15
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:06,000
Om. We meditate on the divine Sun's glorious light;
may it awaken our minds.

16
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:19,200
Revered lady, give me alms.

17
00:12:48,800 --> 00:13:03,000
As rain fallen from the sky makes its way to the sea,
so worship of every god goes on to Keshava.

18
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:14,100
As rain fallen from the sky makes its way to the sea...

19
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:44,000
As rain fallen from the sky
makes its way to the sea,

20
00:14:44,100 --> 00:15:03,000
so worship of every god
goes on to Keshava.

21
00:15:47,500 --> 00:16:02,400
Om. We meditate on the divine Sun's glorious light;
may it awaken our minds. Svaha!

22
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:41,400
Om. We meditate on the divine Sun's glorious light;
may it awaken our minds.

23
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:55,500
Two birds, close companions,
cling to the same tree.

24
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:13,900
One of them eats the sweet fruit;
the other, not eating, simply looks on.

25
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:22,700
The other, not eating, simply looks on.

26
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:47,500
I bow to Parvati and Shiva, parents of the world,
joined like word and meaning, that I may grasp both.

27
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:58,000
At the close of the evening rite
he saw the sage, a treasure of austerity,

28
00:20:10,300 --> 00:20:14,800
with Arundhati beside him,
like the sacred fire with Svaha at its side.

29
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:17,200
Fools disregard Me
when I take on a human form.

30
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:26,800
Revered lady, give me alms.

31
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:45,200
Fruit fallen from the wish-tree of the Veda,
sweetened by nectar from Shuka's lips:

32
00:21:45,300 --> 00:22:04,300
drink deep of the Bhagavata, again and again,
you on earth who know its taste and are moved!

33
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:46,900
Like a bee alighting on a tamala tree in bud,
it rests on Hari, whose body thrills with joy:

34
00:22:51,800 --> 00:23:00,200
that playful sidelong glance, which holds all riches:
may the glance of the goddess of fortune bless me.

35
00:24:13,500 --> 00:24:17,100
Revered lady, give me alms.

36
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:24,600
Revered lady, give me alms.

37
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:33,000
Revered lady, give me alms.

38
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:19,800
Enjoy through renunciation.

39
00:40:07,000 --> 00:40:20,900
A Brahmin guest enters a house like fire itself;
they soothe him so: bring water, O Yama!

40
00:40:21,100 --> 00:40:30,700
Three nights you have stayed in my house unfed,
O Brahmin, a guest worthy of honour.

41
00:40:30,800 --> 00:40:38,500
My homage to you, Brahmin; may all be well with me.
In return, choose three boons.

42
00:40:38,900 --> 00:40:45,700
That my father may be calm and kind of heart,
his anger toward me gone, O Death...

43
00:40:47,800 --> 00:40:54,600
You know the fire that leads to heaven, O Death;
explain it to me, for I have faith.

44
00:40:56,200 --> 00:41:04,500
When a man has died, there is this doubt:
some say he is, and some say he is not.

45
00:41:04,600 --> 00:41:12,800
Taught by you, let me know the truth of it.
Of my boons, this is the third.

46
00:41:13,100 --> 00:41:19,600
Nachiketa, do not question me about death.
Choose another boon.

47
00:41:20,700 --> 00:41:26,500
No other boon is equal to this one.

48
00:41:26,700 --> 00:41:35,200
Choose sons and grandsons to live a hundred years,
cattle in plenty, elephants, gold and horses;

49
00:41:35,300 --> 00:41:43,700
choose a vast estate on the earth,
and live yourself as many autumns as you wish.

50
00:41:43,800 --> 00:41:52,600
No one is ever satisfied by wealth.
Having seen you, we shall have wealth enough;

51
00:41:52,700 --> 00:42:01,300
we shall live as long as you hold sway.
But the boon I choose is that one alone.

52
00:42:01,400 --> 00:42:10,900
This insight is not won by argument;
taught by another, dear one, it is truly understood.

53
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:19,400
You have found it, for you hold fast to truth.
May we always have a questioner like you, Nachiketa!

54
00:44:09,800 --> 00:44:30,600
As rain fallen from the sky makes its way to the sea,
so worship of every god goes on to Keshava.

55
00:45:44,000 --> 00:45:54,500
Tell me who You are, so terrible in form.
I bow to You, greatest of gods: be gracious.

56
00:45:54,600 --> 00:46:05,000
I long to know You, the Primal One,
for I do not understand what You are doing.

57
00:46:17,500 --> 00:46:32,500
Homage to the Arihants, to the Siddhas, to the Acharyas,
to the teachers, and to all the holy ones in the world.

58
00:46:33,400 --> 00:46:58,200
He finds a firm abode, who knows this.
He who knows the abode of the waters...

59
00:51:28,000 --> 00:51:32,700
Established in yoga, do your work, Arjuna,
setting attachment aside.

60
00:53:17,900 --> 00:53:32,300
The glory of Mitra, the god who upholds all peoples,
is true, all-winning, and of the brightest renown.

61
00:53:41,300 --> 00:53:44,300
One may renounce straight from studenthood.

62
00:54:47,700 --> 00:55:00,500
You are the first of gods, the ancient Person,
the final resting place of all this world.

63
00:55:00,600 --> 00:55:13,200
You are the knower and the known, the highest home;
by You, of endless forms, the world is pervaded.

64
00:57:37,300 --> 00:57:41,200
What is unreal never comes to be;
what is real never ceases to be.

65
00:58:13,600 --> 00:58:22,100
The Self is to the south, the Self is to the north;
the Self alone is all this.

66
00:58:22,200 --> 00:58:28,000
One who sees this, who thinks this,
who knows this,

67
00:58:28,100 --> 00:58:37,700
rejoicing in the Self, playing in the Self,
one with it, in its bliss, is his own sovereign.

68
01:04:40,800 --> 01:04:44,500
Only the clay is real.

69
01:05:28,200 --> 01:05:38,400
Satyakama Jabala
once said to his mother, Jabala:

70
01:05:39,400 --> 01:05:47,400
"Mother, I wish to become a student of the Veda.
What is my lineage?"

71
01:07:11,500 --> 01:07:29,900
In my youth I wandered much, a servant girl,
and then I had you.

72
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:37,200
So I do not know
what lineage you are of.

73
01:07:46,300 --> 01:07:49,500
But my name is Jabala,
and your name is Satyakama.

74
01:07:56,000 --> 01:08:03,600
I do not know, sir, what my lineage is.
I asked my mother, and she answered me:

75
01:08:04,200 --> 01:08:11,160
"I do not know it, child. My name is Jabala,
and yours is Satyakama."

76
01:08:11,200 --> 01:08:16,700
So I am Satyakama Jabala, sir.

77
01:08:22,300 --> 01:08:34,000
None but a true Brahmin could speak like this.
Fetch the firewood, my boy: I will initiate you.

78
01:08:34,800 --> 01:08:48,700
A Brahmin has no wealth to match this:
oneness, even-mindedness, and truth.

79
01:11:23,100 --> 01:11:37,600
Be my refuge, Shankara, my teacher.

80
01:11:37,700 --> 01:11:56,900
Master of the nectar-sea of all the scriptures,
treasury of the truths the Upanishads teach,

81
01:11:57,000 --> 01:12:12,400
I hold your spotless feet within my heart:
be my refuge, Shankara, my teacher.

82
01:12:46,000 --> 01:12:56,700
When the appointed hour draws near,
no rule of grammar will save you.

83
01:12:59,300 --> 01:13:13,100
The limbs are worn, the head gone grey,
the mouth now empty of its teeth;

84
01:13:13,200 --> 01:13:27,400
the old man hobbles on a stick,
and still he clutches at his hopes.

85
01:13:30,700 --> 01:13:42,600
Worship Govinda, worship Govinda,
worship Govinda, O foolish mind!

86
01:13:45,100 --> 01:13:56,800
Worship Govinda, worship Govinda,
worship Govinda, O foolish mind!

87
01:13:56,900 --> 01:14:09,100
Worship Govinda, worship Govinda,
worship Govinda, O foolish mind!

88
01:14:10,500 --> 01:14:27,400
Worship Govinda, worship Govinda,
worship Govinda, O foolish mind!

89
01:15:30,800 --> 01:15:44,600
Birth again, and death again,
and again to lie in a mother's womb.

90
01:15:44,800 --> 01:15:59,100
This round of worlds is hard to cross:
in your boundless mercy, save me, Murari!

91
01:16:05,000 --> 01:16:17,500
Worship Govinda, worship Govinda,
worship Govinda, O foolish mind!

92
01:16:51,300 --> 01:16:59,400
As rain fallen from the sky
makes its way to the sea...

93
01:17:30,200 --> 01:17:33,000
Who would delight in a life too long?

94
01:18:45,500 --> 01:18:58,000
Brahman alone am I; and all this world
is but an outspreading of pure Consciousness.

95
01:19:01,400 --> 01:19:05,200
And all of it, without remainder, is conjured by me
through the three-stranded power of ignorance.

96
01:19:05,300 --> 01:19:16,400
He whose conviction stands firm in that
utterly blissful, eternal, supreme, stainless Reality,

97
01:19:26,400 --> 01:19:32,000
be he an outcaste, be he a Brahmin, is my Guru:
this is my firm conviction.

98
01:19:55,800 --> 01:20:06,000
Kashi shines out within Kashi:
Kashi is the light that illumines all.

99
01:20:06,100 --> 01:20:18,900
Whoever has known that Kashi
has truly arrived in Kashi.

100
01:22:01,400 --> 01:22:04,300
Only the clay is real.

101
01:22:33,000 --> 01:22:43,000
The water in the eye is the god of rain,
the pupil is the sun;

102
01:22:43,100 --> 01:22:52,700
its black is fire, its white is Indra,
and through the lower eyelid, the earth attends it.

103
01:23:35,500 --> 01:23:45,200
The One that runs through all things,
yet is touched by none of them,

104
01:23:45,300 --> 01:23:54,800
ever pure and clear like the sky:
I am that Self, whose nature is eternal awareness.

105
01:24:46,000 --> 01:24:52,400
What is night for all beings,
in that the one who is restrained is awake.

106
01:25:46,200 --> 01:25:54,400
Passing to another body, the self goes enveloped:
so the question and the answer show.

107
01:25:58,300 --> 01:26:05,400
It is understood that the soul leaves its former body
and passes into another.

108
01:26:05,600 --> 01:26:15,600
The question is whether it goes
wrapped in the subtle elements, or not.

109
01:26:16,000 --> 01:26:27,200
"Passing to another" means to another body:
it goes forth wrapped in the subtle elements.

110
01:26:27,300 --> 01:26:31,200
How do we know? From the question and the answer.

111
01:26:31,300 --> 01:26:39,500
The question is: "Do you know how, at the fifth offering,
the waters come to be called man?"

112
01:26:39,600 --> 01:26:49,400
And the answer that explains it:
"Thus at the fifth offering the waters are called man."

113
01:27:11,500 --> 01:27:14,700
But water is threefold,
and named for what predominates in it.

114
01:27:16,300 --> 01:27:25,500
That world is a fire, Gautama:
the sun is its fuel, the rays its smoke,

115
01:27:25,600 --> 01:27:34,600
the day its flame, the moon its embers,
the stars its sparks.

116
01:27:34,700 --> 01:27:46,000
Into this fire the gods offer faith;
from that offering King Soma is born.

117
01:27:46,800 --> 01:27:55,900
The rain-cloud is a fire, Gautama:
the wind its fuel, the mist its smoke,

118
01:27:56,000 --> 01:28:02,500
lightning its flame, the thunderbolt its embers,
the rolling thunder its sparks.

119
01:28:02,600 --> 01:28:13,500
Into this fire the gods offer King Soma;
from that offering rain is born.

120
01:28:13,600 --> 01:28:23,300
The earth is a fire, Gautama:
the year its fuel, the sky its smoke,

121
01:28:23,400 --> 01:28:30,900
the night its flame, the four quarters its embers,
the points between them its sparks.

122
01:28:31,000 --> 01:28:40,000
Into this fire the gods offer rain;
from that offering food is born.

123
01:28:40,500 --> 01:28:49,000
Man is a fire, Gautama:
speech its fuel, breath its smoke,

124
01:28:49,100 --> 01:28:56,500
the tongue its flame, the eyes its embers,
the ears its sparks.

125
01:28:56,600 --> 01:29:06,600
Into this fire the gods offer food;
from that offering seed is born.

126
01:29:08,000 --> 01:29:16,400
Woman is a fire, Gautama:
her loins the fuel, the invitation the smoke,

127
01:29:16,500 --> 01:29:25,500
the womb the flame, union the embers,
its pleasures the sparks.

128
01:29:25,600 --> 01:29:34,400
Into this fire the gods offer seed;
from that offering the child in the womb is born.

129
01:29:34,600 --> 01:29:41,500
So it is that, at the fifth offering,
the waters come to be called man.

130
01:29:41,600 --> 01:29:51,200
Wrapped in the caul, the child lies within for ten months,
or nine, or however long, and then is born.

131
01:29:51,300 --> 01:29:55,000
Once born, he lives out his allotted span.

132
01:29:55,100 --> 01:30:03,800
When he has died, they carry him to the fire,
back to where he came from, where he was born.

133
01:35:01,400 --> 01:35:03,700
As rain fallen from the sky...

134
01:36:02,200 --> 01:36:13,300
Homage to the Narmada at dawn and at night;
homage to you, Narmada: guard me from serpents' venom.

135
01:36:13,400 --> 01:36:24,000
The glory of Mitra, the god who upholds all peoples,
is true, all-winning, and of the brightest renown.

136
01:36:27,600 --> 01:36:31,400
Mitra, knowing all, sets the peoples in order...

137
01:38:49,800 --> 01:38:52,900
As long as he lives, he offers the Agnihotra.

138
01:43:33,800 --> 01:43:38,000
Knowing Him thus, one becomes immortal here and now:
there is no other way...

139
01:45:33,800 --> 01:45:36,400
That from which words turn back...

140
01:46:03,400 --> 01:46:22,300
As flowing rivers vanish into the ocean,
leaving behind their names and forms,

141
01:46:25,000 --> 01:46:36,500
so the knower, freed from name and form,
reaches the divine Person, beyond the beyond.

142
01:46:56,200 --> 01:47:26,600
No merit, no sin; no pleasure, no pain;
no mantra, no pilgrimage, no Vedas, no sacrifice.

143
01:47:26,700 --> 01:47:54,400
Not the eating, not the food, not the one who eats:
I am consciousness and bliss. I am Shiva, I am Shiva.

144
01:49:05,000 --> 01:49:22,700
Whose face, arms, feet, waist and eyes are made
of the seven groups of letters, from a to ya:

145
01:49:22,800 --> 01:49:46,000
ruler of all the worlds, eternal, the source of all:
may Sharada grant your minds their purity.

146
01:52:44,700 --> 01:52:53,800
Seven are your fuel-sticks, Agni, seven your tongues,
seven your seers, seven your beloved abodes;

147
01:52:53,900 --> 01:53:03,600
seven priests worship you in seven ways:
fill your seven sources with ghee.

148
02:01:38,200 --> 02:01:59,000
Ever-joyful, granting boons and fearlessness,
sea of beauty, great Goddess who washes sin away,

149
02:01:59,100 --> 02:02:21,000
purifier of the Himalaya's royal line:
Queen of Kashi, gracious Annapurna, give me alms!

150
02:02:33,800 --> 02:02:57,500
Womb of the universe, bearer of all its glories,
who plays out the drama of the world, flame of wisdom,

151
02:02:57,600 --> 02:03:22,900
you who gladden the heart of Vishvanatha:
Queen of Kashi, gracious Annapurna, give me alms!

152
02:03:34,500 --> 02:03:54,000
Bliss of yoga, slayer of foes, upholder of dharma,
bright as sun, moon and fire, guarding the three worlds,

153
02:03:54,100 --> 02:04:14,000
giver of all power, and of the fruit of penance:
Queen of Kashi, gracious Annapurna, give me alms!

154
02:04:24,000 --> 02:04:45,000
Goddess bright with every jewel, Dakshayani, the fair,
gracious, nourishing, loving, goddess of good fortune,

155
02:04:45,100 --> 02:05:05,000
granting the devotee's wish, ever bringing good:
Queen of Kashi, gracious Annapurna, give me alms!

156
02:05:12,500 --> 02:05:35,500
Queen of the earth and all its peoples, sea of mercy,
her hair dark as a braid of blue, giver of daily food,

157
02:05:35,600 --> 02:06:01,500
giver of liberation itself, ever bringing good:
Queen of Kashi, gracious Annapurna, give me alms!

158
02:06:41,700 --> 02:06:43,600
My homeland is the three worlds.

159
02:09:40,500 --> 02:09:56,000
The supreme Self, the One, the first seed of the world,
free of desire, formless, known through Om:

160
02:09:56,100 --> 02:10:13,500
from whom the world is born, by whom it is sustained,
I worship that Lord, in whom the world dissolves.

161
02:11:14,500 --> 02:11:19,500
For those who walk the path beyond the three gunas,
what is enjoined, and what forbidden?

162
02:12:09,500 --> 02:12:20,500
No mother, no father,
no kinsman, no brother;

163
02:12:20,600 --> 02:12:31,900
no wealth, no home:
so wake up, wake up!

164
02:12:32,700 --> 02:12:38,600
So wake up, wake up!

165
02:14:03,800 --> 02:14:21,000
Other gods raise a hand to grant boons and safety;
you alone make no such sign,

166
02:14:21,100 --> 02:14:42,000
for to save from fear, and give more than is wished,
your feet alone suffice, refuge of the worlds.

167
02:19:00,500 --> 02:19:02,900
Breath, truly, is the gatherer.

168
02:19:10,800 --> 02:19:23,000
Speech goes into breath, and the eye, the ear, the mind:
breath gathers all of them into itself.

169
02:21:27,200 --> 02:21:28,800
I am Brahman.

170
02:23:17,600 --> 02:23:33,000
Let my chatter be prayer, every gesture a mudra,
my walking a circling of you, my eating an offering,

171
02:23:33,100 --> 02:23:53,400
my lying down a prostration, all my joys self-giving:
may all that I do become your worship.

172
02:30:19,700 --> 02:30:38,000
Your brow, shining with the pure light of beauty,
seems a second crescent, beside the one in your crown;

173
02:30:43,800 --> 02:30:56,700
set together the other way round, the two would join,
sealed with nectar, into the full moon.

174
02:31:04,000 --> 02:31:21,600
Mountain-born mother, the milk from your heart
is an ocean, I think, of Sarasvati's eloquence;

175
02:31:24,000 --> 02:31:45,000
tasting what you gave in mercy, the Dravida child
became a poet, beloved among the great poets.

176
02:31:55,400 --> 02:31:58,000
Arise! Awake!

177
02:32:57,000 --> 02:33:01,400
Passing beyond this self made of breath...

178
02:34:32,500 --> 02:34:43,000
Only by the grace of God
does the longing for non-duality arise in a person.

179
02:37:25,800 --> 02:37:35,000
Joined to a purified understanding,
mastering himself with steadiness,

180
02:37:35,100 --> 02:37:46,800
letting go of sound and the other objects of sense,
casting off attraction and aversion,

181
02:37:46,900 --> 02:38:04,900
Unattached in mind, self-mastered, free of longing,
he reaches, through renunciation, perfect actionlessness.

182
02:38:05,000 --> 02:38:22,100
Free of ego, force, pride, desire, anger and grasping,
selfless and at peace, he is fit to become Brahman.

183
02:38:56,400 --> 02:39:04,600
As rain fallen from the sky
makes its way to the sea...

184
02:39:04,700 --> 02:39:17,000
As rain fallen from the sky
makes its way to the sea...

185
02:39:21,500 --> 02:39:39,300
That is whole; this is whole;
from the whole, the whole comes forth.

186
02:39:39,400 --> 02:39:48,000
Take the whole from the whole,
and the whole alone remains.
